        "created_at": "2022-09-05T17:26:05.158Z",
        "cooked": "<p>In a game recently, a player had a curse that read something like this:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>After the cursed Cult advances on their summon track, retreat their summon track one space.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>(This is not the exact wording, but a paraphrasing, as I do not have the cards in front of me.)</p>\n<p>So, eventually, the player with that curse advanced her summon track to the victory space, but that also triggered the curse.</p>\n<p>So, my question is: Which is triggered first? The fulfillment of the victory condition, thus letting that player win? Or the curse, thus preventing the player from winning?</p>",
